comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T20:35:40.829Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus3157 with no omissions or unreadable records, request-specific GH-number and semantic searches, current open/in_progress inventories, and full live predecessor data/comments/history. The predecessor scope is delivered; this report names a distinct boundary. New intake is open and unclaimed. Source report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1626"
  "2026-10-30T13:03:37.753Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence: the correction is now derived from runtime contracts rather than a hand list. resolveReadCompletenessControls joins each read-output surface's declared projection modes with the new CliFlagContract.values domain on --depth (get/context brief|standard|deep|full; plan brief|standard|deep). --<level> maps to --depth <level> only when the domain declares the level, --depth <level> maps to --<level> only for a declared projection mode, and --depth standard on a command without --depth replays without the flag. Aliased reads (deps, health) normalise to noun-first argv; the resolver maps item deps/ops health back to the read surface and replays on the canonical path. Same-command operands and globals are preserved. Conflicting --fields/--output-include/--section/--for or a second completeness flag, inline boolean values, and foreign commands get no retry. When no equivalent exists, for example search --depth brief, the refusal lists that command's own controls instead of pointing at other commands. Negative control, using a generated probe over every declaring surface (38 misspellings across 12 surfaces): the pre-fix build d9c4a0bca corrected 7/38; this build corrects 38/38 and every advertised retry executes with exit 0. One probe failure was its own spawnSync 1 MiB buffer on contracts --full, rerun with a larger buffer. Tests: 76 SDK cases generated from PM_READ_OUTPUT_SURFACE_CONTRACTS, plus a CLI integration test that executes one generated correction per surface and checks authoritative tracker bytes are unchanged. ESLint passes; contracts and SDK surface snapshots were updated, with the optional CliFlagContract.values acknowledged as a signature change."
